Upstream bug: cancelled native Responses streams never reach spend logging.
The Chat partial-spend recovery requires collected chunks that Responses
iterators do not expose, and cancellation bypasses ordinary failure hooks.

Related upstream tracking (these do not cover this native Responses path):
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/14457
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/33736
https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/pull/35349

Record the cancellation as a 499 failure through native failure callbacks and
the proxy failure hook, which persists the row and releases the request slot.
Delivered output text becomes a logging-only cancelled Response snapshot in
the standard failure payload, so redaction and prompt-storage settings apply;
final usage stays unknown. The Logs drawer shows that captured output instead
of replacing every failed response with the error object.

Removal checks: tests/verify_responses_disconnect.py and
tests/verify_responses_disconnect_ui.integration.test.tsx against unpatched upstream,
then cancel a native Responses stream and verify one 499 row with partial output
in the Logs UI, preserved after refresh.

